# Configuration

Settings come from flags and environment variables. Flags win; an empty or
blank variable uses the default. The program doesn't load `.env` files;
`.env.example` lists every variable.

| Flag | Variable | Default | Validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--tasks FILE` | `{{env_prefix}}_TASKS` | unset: the built-in sample | A readable JSON array of `{id, title, status, notes}`; ids present and unique, titles present, status `todo`, `doing` or `done`, no other keys |
| `--log-file FILE` | `{{env_prefix}}_LOG_FILE` | unset: no logs | Its directory must exist; records are appended as JSON lines. Not the tasks file |
| `--no-tui` | `{{env_prefix}}_NO_TUI` | `false` | `true`, `false`, `1` or `0`. Print the tasks as text and exit |
| `--json` | | off | Print `{"tasks": [...]}` (or the version, or help) as JSON; errors become `{"error": {...}}` on stderr |
| `--version` | | | Print the version |
| `--help` | | | Print usage |

Relative paths resolve from the working directory. The full-screen UI runs only
when neither `--no-tui` nor `--json` is set and both stdin and stdout are
terminals; otherwise the program prints and exits.

`RUST_LOG` (tracing's filter syntax, such as `debug` or `{{project_slug}}=trace`)
sets the log level, default `info`. An invalid value fails with exit status 3
even without a log file.

## Exit status

| Status | Code | When |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | | Success, including `--help`, `--version` and quitting the UI with `q` or ctrl+c |
| 1 | `IO`, `INVALID_DATA`, `TERMINAL` | The tasks file is unreadable or invalid, the terminal failed, or output couldn't be written |
| 2 | `USAGE` | Unknown flag or bad argument |
| 3 | `INVALID_SETTING`, `LOG_FILE` | A bad environment value or `RUST_LOG`, or a log file that can't be opened |

Every failure prints `error[CODE]: message` and a `suggestion:` line on stderr,
or one JSON document under `--json`.

## Adding a setting

Give it a flag in `src/cli.rs` and `Flags`, its variable and validation in
`config::load`, a test in `config.rs`, and a row in this file and
`.env.example`.
